Public Hearing to determine whether compliance of annexation conditions required by
Wyoming Statute §15-1-402 exist for a parcel of approximately 1.78 acres of land situated in Tracts
45 and 46, Dell Range Addition, 4th Filing, Laramie County, Wyoming (located on the northeast
corner of N. College Drive and Dell Range Boulevard).  Josh Tetzlaff, Planning and Development
office, advised the proposed annexation is pursuant to a petition requesting annexation submitted
by the property owner; briefly reviewed the area to be annexed, and stated that requirements and
compliance of annexation conditions contained in state statutes had been met.  Upon inquiry, Mr.
Tetzlaff stated his belief that one property owner will be involved in development plans, and that
preliminary discussions suggest potential plans may be redevelopment of the property for medical
offices.  There being no further comments or input and purpose of the hearing having been met,
Mayor Kaysen closed the public hearing.
Public Hearing to determine whether compliance of annexation conditions required by
Wyoming Statute §15-1-402 exist for a parcel of approximately 17,268 square feet of land situated
in Lots 11 and 12, Block 1, Downey Addition, Laramie County, Wyoming (located north of and
adjacent to Land Court, east of Grove Drive).  Josh Tetzlaff, Planning and Development office,
advised the proposed annexation is pursuant to a petition requesting annexation submitted by the
property owner; briefly reviewed the area to be annexed, and stated that requirements and
compliance of annexation conditions contained in state statutes had been met. There being no further
comments or input and purpose of the hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the public
hearing.
ORDINANCE - Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a portion of the NW1/4 of
Section 21, T.14N., R.66W., 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming, to be known as The Bluffs, 10th
Filing Annexation (located between Converse Avenue and Crestridge Drive, north of Foothills Road)
(Postponed from January 26, 2015).  Kelly Hafner, Benchmark Engineering, agent for the applicant
and property owner, United Western Corporation, expressed appreciation to Dan White, City
Attorney, for providing feedback to him following discussion at Public Services Committee, and
requested a two week postponement to keep the timing for the affiliated final plat and re-zoning
actions together and allow for an additional matter to be worked out.  Reporting for Public Services
Committee, Mr. Cook moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Mr.
Cook, seconded by Mr. Shanor, moved to amend by replacing the current language in Section 5 of
the ordinance with the following language:  “That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect
upon its approval and publication and upon the official filing of the affiliated The Bluffs, 10 Filing,
th
final plat map with the County Clerk and Ex-Officio Register of Deeds for Laramie County,
Wyoming.”.  Upon inquiry regarding purpose of the amendment, Mr. Hafner explained the
amendment wording was requested at Committee to keep the annexation, zone change and final plat
```

### Page 3 of 8

```text
all together relative to effective date of the annexation.  He explained there was a concern that if the
plat didn’t get recorded then they would not want the annexation and zone change to be effective.
Mr. Hafner advised Mr. White had offered him an opinion since the Committee meeting that he felt
the statutes require an annexation ordinance be tied to a date but not tied to filing of a particular
document to become effective, and requested the amendment be voted down so further discussion
could occur.  Upon inquiry, Dan White, City Attorney, advised it is not customary to state an
annexation ordinance becomes effective upon the approval of an affiliated final plat. He noted the
ordinance is usually effective either when it is published or, in addition, on a date specified in the
annexation.  Mr. White stated continuing discussions with Mr. Hafner will be held to review a
potential way to address the applicant’s concern.  Upon further inquiry, Mr. White advised he will
review statutes to determine whether the amendment wording, which is currently contained in the
affiliated re-zoning ordinance, was applicable.  Comment followed regarding an annexation action
being a separate issue from a final plat or zone change since annexation serves as an initial starting
point.  Motion to amend failed.  Voting “no” -- all members of the governing body.  Mr. Shanor
moved to postpone to February 23, 2015, seconded by Ms. Williams.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes”
-- all members of the governing body.
AN ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2,
Zoning Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Unified Development
Code, changing the zoning classification from County LR Low Density Residential and LR-2 Low
Density Residential, Developing to MR-2 Medium-Density Residential, Developing for Cheyenne,
Wyoming, The Bluffs, 10th Filing (located north of and adjacent to Foothills Road between Point
Bluff and Mountain Road).  Kelly Hafner, Benchmark Engineering, agent for the applicant and
property owner, United Western Corporation, requested a two week postponement in order to tie the
zone change with the approval time frame of the annexation.  Mr. Cook moved to approve on third
and final reading, seconded by Ms. Williams.  Mr. Cook moved to postpone to February 23, 2015,
seconded by Mr. Shanor.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2, Zoning
Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Cheyenne Unified Development
Code, changing the zoning classification from CB Community Business to MUB Mixed Use
Business Emphasis for Lot 2, Block 1, Triumph Addition, 2nd Filing, Cheyenne, Wyoming (located
north of and adjacent to Grand Harmony Boulevard, west of Center Drive).  Mr. Cook moved to
approve on second reading, seconded by Mr. Johnson.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members
of the governing body.
ORDINANCE - Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a portion of the W1/2 E1/2
of Section 35, T.14N., R.66W., 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming, to be known as Chukker
Ridge, 2nd Filing Annexation (located east of Pennsylvania Avenue, between 13th Street and
Atlantic Avenue) -- referred to Public Services Committee (sponsor -- Mr. Cook).
